From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 08:53:16 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: mt5806: wait for the IC's post-start interrupt
 in suspend

The first s2idle after the pen charger driver had loaded was aborted
(area-combo-99, kernel q80, cycle bfpcie-base-1): the suspend began while
the driver's start sequence was running (hBoost request, 1 s power cycle,
2.5 s wake), the device suspend blocked on the driver's mutex until the
sequence ended ("suspend of devices complete after 2250.028 msecs"), and
104 ms after the sequence the IC raised its interrupt line - 1 ms after
dpm_suspend_noirq() had armed the wake-up interrupts. The line is a
wake-up source ("wakeup-source" in the device tree, as stock's
enable_irq_wake()), so the kernel treated the edge as a wake-up event:
"PM: Triggering wakeup from IRQ 316", 4.5 s wall time for an 8 s alarm,
no CX collapse. The two following cycles were clean. IRQ 316 is the pen
charger's line (TLMM GPIO 169; its number depends on the udev load order:
314 / 297 / 296 / 306 in runs 96 / 92 / 89 / 87).

An edge that arrives before suspend_device_irqs() is handled, or latched
and replayed at the resume; the same edge after it aborts the suspend.
So the suspend callback now waits for a running start sequence
(flush_work() - a retry that is merely scheduled stays scheduled) and
then until the IC's interrupt must have come (1 s after the sequence, or
after the power cycle that follows a transfer error, which ends with the
same wake line edge), before it disables the interrupt and the PM core
goes on to arm the wake-up interrupts.

Stock holds a wakeup source through its init_work_func instead
(oplus_mt5806.c:4370, :4405). That aborts a suspend early only through
the wakeup_count protocol Android uses; a plain write to /sys/power/state
(systemd, the kit tests) does not look at wakeup sources
(pm_wakeup_pending(): events_check_enabled), so the wait in the suspend
callback is the equivalent here. The cost is at most 1 s added to a
suspend that falls into the start sequence; a suspend at any other time
is unchanged.

Tested on the OnePlus Pad 4 (area-combo-104, kernel q83): the driver
bound and an s2idle requested at once - woken by the RTC alarm after
21.3 s (alarm 20 s), CX collapsed for 76 % of the sleep (cxsd +14), the
device suspend waited 3.46 s for the start sequence, no wake-up from the
pen charger's line ("first: FIXED"); the second sleep clean (cxsd +5,
83 %). Before the change (area-combo-99, cycle base-1) the same first
sleep was aborted after 4.5 s with cxsd +0.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/mt5806_pen_charger.c | 32 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 32 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/mt5806_pen_charger.c b/drivers/power/supply/mt5806_pen_charger.c
index f450871bce4a..78523bc9a7f1 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/mt5806_pen_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/mt5806_pen_charger.c
@@ -135,6 +135,7 @@
 /* a failed start (no confirmed supply, no answer of the IC) is tried again a few times */
 #define MT5806_INIT_RETRIES		3
 #define MT5806_INIT_RETRY_MS		10000
+#define MT5806_IRQ_GRACE_MS		1000	/* the IC's interrupt ~100 ms after a power-up (area-combo-99) */
 
 /* PMIC GLINK: stock oplus_wireless_pen_glink.h:15-28 */
 #define MT5806_HBOOST_OWNER		32785
@@ -256,6 +257,7 @@ struct mt5806 {
 	bool removing;
 	bool suspended;
 	bool suspend_off;
+	unsigned long irq_due;			/* jiffies until which the IC's post-power-up interrupt is expected */
 	const char *fail;
 
 	bool tx_allowed;
@@ -642,6 +644,18 @@ static void mt5806_boost_request(struct mt5806 *chip, u32 mv)
 	schedule_work(&chip->boost_work);
 }
 
+/*
+ * After a power-up of the IC (the start sequence, the power cycle after an
+ * error) its interrupt line falls once more about 100 ms after the sequence
+ * has ended (area-combo-99, cycle base-1). mt5806_suspend() waits that out:
+ * an edge taken before the interrupts are armed for wake-up is handled or
+ * latched for the resume, the same edge after that aborts the suspend.
+ */
+static void mt5806_expect_irq(struct mt5806 *chip)
+{
+	WRITE_ONCE(chip->irq_due, jiffies + msecs_to_jiffies(MT5806_IRQ_GRACE_MS));
+}
+
 /* stock mt_wls_reset_sys (c:1366-1384), with the transmitter held off */
 static void mt5806_ic_reset(struct mt5806 *chip)
 {
@@ -653,6 +667,7 @@ static void mt5806_ic_reset(struct mt5806 *chip)
 	gpiod_set_value_cansleep(chip->enable_gpio, 1);
 	msleep(MT5806_WAKE_MS);
 	gpiod_set_value_cansleep(chip->wake_gpio, 0);
+	mt5806_expect_irq(chip);
 }
 
 static void mt5806_on_attach(struct mt5806 *chip)
@@ -1079,6 +1094,7 @@ static void mt5806_init_work(struct work_struct *work)
 	mt5806_handle_events(chip);
 	gpiod_set_value_cansleep(chip->wake_gpio, 0);		/* c:4395 */
 	mt5806_tx_update(chip);					/* c:4396 */
+	mt5806_expect_irq(chip);
 
 	dev_info(chip->dev, "MT5806 firmware 0x%x, supply %u mV, transmitter %s\n",
 		 chip->fw_version, chip->boost_acked_mv,
@@ -1533,6 +1549,22 @@ static void mt5806_shutdown(struct i2c_client *client)
 static int mt5806_suspend(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct mt5806 *chip = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+	unsigned long due;
+
+	/*
+	 * A start sequence that is still running ends with the transmitter
+	 * enabled and an interrupt of the IC about 100 ms later; the power cycle
+	 * after an error does the same. Wait for both before the interrupts are
+	 * armed for wake-up (dpm_suspend_noirq): an edge taken now is handled or
+	 * latched for the resume, the same edge in the noirq phase aborts the
+	 * suspend (area-combo-99: "PM: Triggering wakeup from IRQ 316" in the
+	 * first s2idle after the driver had loaded). flush_work() waits for a
+	 * running start only; a retry that is merely scheduled stays scheduled.
+	 */
+	flush_work(&chip->init_work.work);
+	due = READ_ONCE(chip->irq_due);
+	if (time_before(jiffies, due))
+		msleep(jiffies_to_msecs(due - jiffies));
 
 	disable_irq(chip->irq);
 
-- 
2.43.0

